# Installed to /etc/sudoers.d/docker-daemon (mode 0440, root:root).
# Jellyfin-gated Docker lifecycle: ethan's "Jellyfin Server" launcher starts the
# daemon on demand, and the jellyfin-daemon-guard user service stops it again when
# the jellyfin container dies (driven from Jellyfin's Dashboard -> Shut Down).
# The guard runs unattended (a background systemd --user service) so it cannot type
# a password -- hence NOPASSWD, scoped to exactly these two invocations, nothing else.
# See my-system: users-and-permissions/sudo-policy.md and services/docker.md.
ethan ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl start docker.service
ethan ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl stop docker.service docker.socket
